(Discrepancy 3: LANGUAGE.md:627-629 lists the target of `Allocate ... for`
 among the bindings that reject a conflicting type. A buffer target is let
 through, and the allocation silently replaces the buffer's capacity with 0 —
 an 8-byte buffer becomes a 0-byte one with no diagnostic. A text or list
 target IS rejected (see VAR-37), so the check exists; the buffer case
 escapes it.
